   prompt|
   prompt| Work chat quick help:
   prompt| 💬 Work chat advanced help
   prompt| `helper status` or `!status` - check progress
   prompt| `helper stats` or `!stats` - show Codex token usage by model/service-tier combination, cache/context analysis, and rate-limit metadata when Codex recorded it
   prompt| `helper details` or `!details` - show IDs and debug details
   prompt| `helper rename <title>` or `!rename <title>` - rename this Teams chat
   prompt| `helper rename hostname <name>` - rename this machine in all related chat titles
   prompt| `helper file <relative-path>` or `!file <relative-path>` - upload a file prepared in the helper's Teams upload folder
   prompt| `helper close` or `!close` - close this Codex session in Teams
   prompt| `helper park <session-number-or-id>` / `helper resume <session-number-or-id>` / `helper unpark <session-number-or-id>` - manually pause or resume polling for a Work chat
   prompt| `helper unpause` - resume auto-start after a pause (requests sent while paused are not run)
   prompt| `helper fork` - copy this session into a new Work chat
   prompt| `helper goal` / `helper goal <objective>` / `helper goal active` / `helper goal pause` - show, set, resume or pause this chat's Codex goal (Codex keeps working on an active goal by itself; `helper cancel` pauses it)
   prompt| `helper publish-history` or `!ph` - import a paused local Codex history backlog
   prompt| `helper publish-history full` - publish the complete local Codex history once to this chat
   prompt| `helper queue <prompt>` - enqueue a separate task; the prompt is kept as text, including helper commands
   prompt| advanced commands: `helper retry last`, `helper retry <turn-id>` / `!retry <turn-id>`, or `helper cancel last`, `helper cancel queued`, `helper cancel running`, `helper cancel all`, `helper cancel <turn-id>` / `!cancel <turn-id>`
   prompt| Status words: `queued`/`running` means wait, `completed` means done, `failed` or `interrupted` means check recent messages and changed files before `helper retry last`.
